<h2>Implementation</h2>
<p>Getting all of that to behave took most of my time. Working in the developers' Blueprints, I:</p>
<ul class="points">
  <li>synced sounds to animation frames, and gave Lulu's landings a different sound for each surface (wood, metal grate, cardboard, milk crate and more) by checking the physics material under her as she lands</li>
  <li>hooked sounds onto the developers' timelines, so vans rev up as they set off and moving platforms only hum while they're moving</li>
  <li>used child Blueprints so each kind of box has its own push sound, fading with distance</li>
  <li>added audio volumes so the reverb and ambience change between indoors and out</li>
  <li>stopped sounds doubling up with concurrency rules and do-once gates</li>
</ul>

